# The alarm machinery's own state store, split out of the documents it files on 2026-09-24.
#
# UNTRACKED IS THE WHOLE POINT, not a convenience. A repeating-alarm document used to be three
# things at once -- the state store, the published work item, and a tracked path origin carries
# its own copy of -- and any two of those are fine while all three are a self-refilling
# FF_MODIFIED collision. On 2026-09-24 the shared tree sat ten commits behind origin/main with
# the fast-forward refused on nine of these documents, and its daemons were running code 55
# modules behind as a result. This file is where the state went so the documents could become a
# rendering that clearing costs nothing.
#
# If this line is ever dropped, the collision comes back within a day: the store is rewritten by
# every firing of every alarm family, which on this box is several times an hour.
docs/observability/.alarm_repetition_state.json
# Same shape, same reason: rewritten by every reconcile-watch tick (five minutes), and it
# holds one stamp that means nothing outside this box's own alarm memory.
docs/observability/.fork_open_streak.json
docs/observability/injection-log.jsonl
docs/staging/**/*.bak
